
. *! qa/replay/pipeline.do  version 1.0.0  09aug2026
. * A golden master for the fixture pipeline: run the three stages and print the
. * statistics they produce.  Blessed against qa/replay/pipeline.log.
. *
. * Why this pair exists.  INT-11..13 assert that the stages return cleanly, tha
> t
. * the output dataset is written, and that the constructed indicator is a
. * proportion -- all of which stay true of a pipeline that has started computin
> g
. * something else entirely.  This pair pins the NUMBERS, so a change in the
. * stages surfaces as output drift instead of as a still-passing shape check.
. * That is the division of labour the package argues for: assertions say what
. * must hold, a blessed master says what was.
. *
. * Determinism.  01_import.do seeds the generator, and every path printed here
. * is relative, so the log reproduces on another machine -- the two conditions
. * stqa_replay's contract enforces at blessing time.  Stata's random-number
. * stream is version-dependent; the version gate handles that by SKIPping when
. * the replaying Stata differs from the blessing one, rather than reporting
. * drift that is really a different Stata.
. *
. * No verdict tokens are emitted here on purpose.  A replayed do-file's output
. * reaches the parent case log, and a line-initial PASS or FAIL token would be
. * counted by the log scanner as a verdict of the suite that replayed it.
. *
. * Nor does this file spell those two tokens with a slash between them.  The
. * determinism contract rejects a drive-absolute path with "[A-Za-z]:[/\]", and
. * that pattern matches ordinary prose joining the two words with a slash -- th
> e
. * first blessing of this master was refused for exactly that, on this comment.
. * The over-match is conservative (it refuses a good log rather than blessing a
. * bad one) and is logged for the next package revision.
. * Author: Joao Pedro Azevedo (UNICEF)
. 
. * The stages write into gitignored scratch, which therefore does not exist in 
> a
. * fresh clone. test_pipeline.do creates it -- but it runs AFTER test_manifest.
> do
. * alphabetically, so leaning on that neighbour makes this master pass in a tre
> e
. * that has run the suite before and fail on any clean checkout. It did exactly
. * that: green here, r(603) on the public clone. A golden master that depends o
> n
. * the order its neighbours happen to run in is not a golden master.
. capture mkdir "qa/fixtures/pipeline/output"

. 
. quietly do "qa/fixtures/pipeline/01_import.do"

. quietly do "qa/fixtures/pipeline/02_clean.do"

. quietly do "qa/fixtures/pipeline/03_construct.do"

. 
. use "qa/fixtures/pipeline/output/indicators.dta", clear

. 
. quietly count

. display "observations   : " r(N)
observations   : 100

. 
. quietly summarize value

. display "value mean     : " %6.4f r(mean)
value mean     : 0.5445

. display "value min      : " %6.4f r(min)
value min      : 0.0057

. display "value max      : " %6.4f r(max)
value max      : 0.9879

. 
. quietly summarize indicator_value

. display "indicator mean : " %6.4f r(mean)
indicator mean : 0.5300

. 
. quietly count if indicator_value == 1

. display "indicator ones : " r(N)
indicator ones : 53

. 
. display "PIPELINE REPLAY COMPLETE"
PIPELINE REPLAY COMPLETE

. 
end of do-file
